,[-527.9,-1142.6],[-521.8,-1150.5],[-517.3,-1159.3],[-513.5,-1168.6],[-509.8,-1177.9],[-509.9,-1187.8],[-510.1,-1197.8],[-508.6,-1207.7],[-505.8,-1217.2],[-501.3,-1226.1],[-496.7,-1235.0],[-495.3,-1244.3],[-497.8,-1254.0],[-499.8,-1263.7],[-499.7,-1273.7],[-494.9,-1282.4],[-490.0,-1291.2],[-483.8,-1298.8],[-476.2,-1305.3],[-468.7,-1311.9],[-461.6,-1319.0],[-455.7,-1327.0],[-452.4,-1336.2],[-451.1,-1346.1],[-448.8,-1355.8],[-445.7,-1365.3],[-441.7,-1374.4],[-437.7,-1383.6],[-432.9,-1392.3],[-426.8,-1400.2],[-419.9,-1407.4],[-412.8,-1414.4],[-405.3,-1421.1],[-397.7,-1427.5],[-390.3,-1434.2],[-384.1,-1442.1],[-379.1,-1450.7],[-372.6,-1458.0],[-364.8,-1464.3],[-357.5,-1471.0],[-352.5,-1479.2],[-352.3,-1489.2],[-352.2,-1493.9]]},{"kind":"stream","name":null,"pts":[[-123.0,-1493.0],[-114.0,-1490.0],[-111.1,-1491.9]]},{"kind":"stream","name":null,"pts":[[-8.9,-1469.4],[-18.6,-1471.7],[-28.4,-1473.9],[-38.0,-1476.5],[-47.4,-1479.9],[-56.8,-1483.3],[-65.2,-1488.7],[-71.6,-1492.8]]},{"kind":"stream","name":null,"pts":[[-177.1,-1433.8],[-169.2,-1440.0],[-161.3,-1446.1],[-153.2,-1451.9],[-144.4,-1456.7],[-135.6,-1461.5],[-126.8,-1466.1],[-117.6,-1470.1],[-113.0,-1478.0]]}],"facts":{"drive_km":0.6,"drive_start_m":879,"drive_end_m":886,"drive_climb_m":11,"drive_max_grade_pct":5,"drive_minutes_at_9kmh":4,"box_km":[3.04,2.99],"arrival_m":886},"edits":["A bench up to 24 m wide is cut along the jeep track to its smoothed profile (the 30 m DSM includes tree canopy).","Road bumps and ruts in the drive are illustrative; the grade and the line of the jeep track are real.","Trees, shrubs, grass tufts and boulders are placed where WorldCover maps that cover; their size and number are illustrative.","The walking loop is a 16 m circle around the arrival point; it is not a mapped trail.","The boulder is drawn (no source gives its size or shape): about 12 m wide, 6 m high and 8 m deep, a weathered granite block leaning back about 30 degrees, its centre set 4 m west and 4 m south of the place point (so it stands clear of the lane), its base sunk 1 m into the real DEM slope; no levelled terrace (terrace 0). Its colour (granite with lichen-ochre patches) is estimated from the photos.","The incised figures are drawn after photos Zainul Abideen and Yusra.Amin123 (Commons, CC BY-SA 4.0): a row of animal outlines with horns or necks, a few human-like figures, a spoked wheeled form, and dots and rings, as thin pale lines about 18% lighter than the rock (drawn after photos). Their number, size and places are estimated from the photos, not measured.","The sources give a chariot only in one line (Livius: 'the animals and chariots'); the drawn wheeled form is after that line and the photos, not measured.","The sources give 'more than 100 carvings' and 71 animals, 17 objects and 29 unidentified (Olivieri, via Dawn); the drawing shows a sample, not all of them. The Dawn article could not be fetched here (HTTP 403), so these counts are unverified.","The Buddhist relief (sixth century CE, Livius) is not visible in the photos used and is not drawn.","The face is turned to the end of the drive (no compass bearing is given in any source); the photos show the cliff, not its orientation.","The village lanes that bring the visitor here are OSM roads; the N-95 Mingora road is about 0.46 km off, so the drive takes the lanes from the junction and stops at the rock.","The 18 buildings stand on their OSM footprints; their height (OSM levels where mapped, else one or two storeys), roofs and colours are illustrative, after visitors' photos.","Season colours, snow, ice and dawn mist are illustrative.","Traffic on the drive is illustrative: the vehicle kinds are those seen on Swat roads (Willys jeeps, Hilux, Suzuki vans, Mehran cars, CD70 motorbikes, Qingqi rickshaws, painted trucks); their number and movement are not counted."],"sources":[{"name":"Copernicus DEM GLO-30","use":"terrain heights","licence":"© DLR e.V. 2010-2014 and © Airbus Defence and Space GmbH 2014-2018, provided under COPERNICUS by the European Union and ESA","url":"https://spacedata.copernicus.eu/collections/copernicus-digital-elevation-model"},{"name":"ESA WorldCover 10 m 2021 v200","use":"trees, meadow, rock, snow","licence":"CC BY 4.0, © ESA WorldCover project 2021","url":"https://esa-worldcover.org"},{"name":"Livius.org (Jona Lendering), Gogdara","use":"location (just off the main road in a small village), c.1000 BCE dating of the petroglyphs, the sixth-century CE Buddhist addition, the 'animals and chariots' line","licence":"text quoted for the practical facts; all rights with the author","url":"https://www.livius.org/articles/place/gogdara/"},{"name":"Xplore Open heritage database, Gogdara Rock Carvings","use":"more than 100 carvings on a rocky cliff; animals, humans, geometric patterns and inscriptions; dating 2nd century BCE to 5th century CE; free entry; hamlet of Udegram","licence":"text quoted; the database lists CC BY SA","url":"https://xploreopen.org/heritage_sites/gogdara-rock-carvings/"},{"name":"Dawn, 'Rock carving depicts ancient lifestyle of Swat'","use":"71 animal, 17 object and 29 unidentified graffiti (Olivieri); rock at the foot of the northern slopes of Mt Sakhi-sar; early first millennium BCE","licence":"news text, all rights with Dawn","url":"https://www.dawn.com/news/1447677"},{"name":"Wikimedia Commons photos (Gogdara Rock Carvings)","use":"the six reference photos the drawn figures follow","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","url":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rock_carvings_-_Gogdara.jpg"},{"name":"OpenStreetMap","use":"the residential lanes from the N-95 junction to the rock (no surface tagged); the N-95 Mingora road 0.46 km off and the village buildings","licence":"ODbL, © OpenStreetMap contributors","url":"https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright"}]}